From ef6c10693890b7ba5f590e5babbf215c3f0857f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Max (Muse)" <max@local.prototype>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 01:12:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Move time-capsule date picker into connection setup

The TEMPORAL DESTINATION menu now runs at the end of
startup_configuration(), alongside the baud rate and other terminal
options, instead of after login. All non-service (meta) choices live in
one place; once on the service, everything stays period-authentic.

- New choose_temporal_destination_setup(): same 1-4 menu, pre-login.
  The raw choice is stashed in pending_simulation_date (date, None, or a
  surprise sentinel) since the account isn't known yet.
- New apply_pending_simulation_date(): runs post-login where the old
  prompt was. Applies explicit choices directly, resolves 'surprise'
  with the per-user seed, and keeps the per-account 'Return to <date>?'
  shortcut for 'Present Day' picks. Persists last_simulation_date and
  sets SessionState.simulation_date exactly as before.
- Removed the old post-login choose_temporal_destination().
